					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13226023#post-4589402</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13226023/lte-8686-yellow-kewpie#post-4589402</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2020 22:13:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Nagiros</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4665703</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm not really seeing much going on here — I like the little world-building of the Foundation redesignating slots<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-656116-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>, but everything here just comes off as kind of predictable. There's no larger twist or subversion, I guess.</p> <p>And I don't want to be abrasive, but the inclusion of references to the Decom. Department beyond a name drop seem superfluous. They don't add anything to the article in my mind. There's a sort of horror that can be derived here, of the line between Foundation and GOC dogma being blurred, but it's not really&#8230; executed in this article. I think.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-656116-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Which has been a thing since, like, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-048">SCP-048</a>, but it's cool to see it again.</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
